<title>GERMANY: EU backs east German shipyard subsidies - report.</title>
<headline>EU backs east German shipyard subsidies - report.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission will give its backing to German government plans to provide a massive subsidy to east German shipyards, Focus magazine said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Focus said that the commission would recommend to the council of ministers early next week that a subsidy of 1.04 billion marks be provided to the shipyards.</p>
<p>In exchange for the EU's approval, Germany must promise to limit capacity at the shipyards until the end of 2000.</p>
<p>The German economics ministry was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>The magazine said that MTW-Schiffswerft Wismar will get 450 million marks of support and that Volkswerft Stralsund will receive 590 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
